# Variant tiers-2026-09-24 — every tier on Opus 5.5, which defaults to `medium`: mid at `medium`,
# strong at `high`, max at `xhigh`. Every Opus result in benchmark.md is from Opus 5 (the run
# logs show `claude-opus-5`), so this re-measures the tiers on the new model.
# Start it with `--base 8678ab31`, the commit where variant a's step 2 ended, so step 3 begins
# from the same code as the step-3 arms before it; steps 1 and 2 are already shipped there.
# Step 3 only (`--to 3`) compares the strong tier. The mid tier (Opus at `medium` against
# variant c's Fable at `medium`) needs its own run of steps 1–2 from the benchmark base.
# Judge on, as in s3-opus-high, so the findings compare.
# Protocol and earlier results: scripts/plan-runner/benchmark.md
MODEL_MAX=opus
EFFORT_MAX=xhigh
ADVISOR_MAX=
MODEL_STRONG=opus
EFFORT_STRONG=high
ADVISOR_STRONG=
MODEL_MID=opus
EFFORT_MID=medium
ADVISOR_MID=
JUDGE_MODEL=opus
JUDGE_EFFORT=high
